{
  "_comment": "Copy the block for your harness to its config location and drop the _comment/_locations/_notes keys. OpenCode does NOT use the top-level block below — see _opencode.",
  "_locations": {
    "antigravity-global":   "~/.config/antigravity/mcp.json",
    "antigravity-per-repo": ".antigravity/mcp.json  (repo root)",
    "vscode-copilot":       ".vscode/mcp.json  (repo root)",
    "claude-code":          "~/.claude/mcp.json  (global)",
    "opencode-global":      "~/.config/opencode/opencode.json",
    "opencode-per-repo":    "opencode.json  (repo root)"
  },
  "powerbi-modeling-mcp": {
    "type": "stdio",
    "command": "npx",
    "args": ["-y", "@microsoft/powerbi-modeling-mcp@latest", "--start"],
    "_notes": [
      "Requires Node.js 18+ and npx on PATH.",
      "On Windows: connects to a running Power BI Desktop instance automatically.",
      "On Linux: connects to a Fabric workspace or a PBIP/TMDL folder on disk. The MCP server will prompt for auth on first use.",
      "See https://github.com/microsoft/powerbi-modeling-mcp for full docs."
    ]
  },

  "_opencode": {
    "_comment": "OpenCode V2 uses a different schema: servers nest under mcp.servers, type is 'local' (not 'stdio'), and command is a single array of executable + args. Add the whole _opencode block below into your opencode.json.",
    "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
    "mcp": {
      "timeout": {
        "startup": 180000
      },
      "servers": {
        "powerbi": {
          "type": "local",
          "command": ["npx", "-y", "@microsoft/powerbi-modeling-mcp@latest", "--start"]
        }
      }
    },
    "_notes": [
      "timeout.startup is raised to 180s because the first npx run downloads a .NET binary; the default 30s startup timeout is not enough on a cold cache.",
      "Install globally with: opencode mcp add powerbi --global -- npx -y @microsoft/powerbi-modeling-mcp@latest --start",
      "A project-level server with the same name REPLACES the global one entirely (not merged), so keep the entry in one place only."
    ]
  },

  "_shared_cautions": [
    "Register either the local server or the hosted server, never both. Overlapping tool sets make routing ambiguous and waste tokens on every request. Hosted = https://api.fabric.microsoft.com/v1/mcp/powerbi/authoring (Fabric workspaces only; it cannot reach Power BI Desktop or PBIP files on disk).",
    "Model edits are held in the server's memory. Changes are NOT written to .tmdl files until you explicitly run database_operations -> ExportToTmdlFolder. Committing before that export loses the work.",
    "Keep the PBIP under Git so every change is a reviewable diff and revertable.",
    "Add --readonly to args to block all write operations, or --authmode=serviceprincipal with AZURE_CLIENT_ID / AZURE_TENANT_ID / AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET for CI."
  ]
}
